## Why This Is Asked
This questions probes real-world, end-to-end tenant isolation in ML pipelines, focusing on runtime IAM decisions and breach containment.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Studio isolation in multi-tenant environments
- Per-tenant KMS keys with rotation
- Explicit cross-account trusts using conditions and tags
- PrivateLink data access patterns
- Immutable, multi-region CloudTrail
- Secrets rotation and automated credential revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo Node.js AWS SDK snippet for revoking tenant access after a breach
const AWS = require('aws-sdk');
const iam = new AWS.IAM();
async function revokeTenant(tenantId){
  // Remove the cross-account trust or revoke temporary credentials
  await iam.deleteRolePolicy({ RoleName: `sage_${tenantId}_exec`, PolicyName: 'AssumeRole' }).catch(() => {});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test containment within 60 seconds?
- How would you rotate per-tenant KMS keys without disrupting workloads?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates expertise in architecting secure, scalable data science environments with strict least-privilege controls across multi-account data lakes, requiring mastery of ABAC, Lake Formation, KMS, and private networking.

## Key Concepts
- Attribute-based access control (ABAC) with IAM policy tags
- Lake Formation fine-grained permissions
- SageMaker notebook cross-account trust relationships
- Private connectivity through VPC endpoints
- Centralized CMK with rotation policies
- Immutable audit logging via CloudTrail
- Automated drift and privilege-creep detection

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::data-lake/${aws:PrincipalTag/project}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:ExistingObjectTag/dataset": "${aws:PrincipalTag/dataset}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```
